IMPORT prelude

-- Point-to-Point Passenger Transport Industry Act 2019 (Singapore) -- what a street-hail (taxi) service and a ride-hail service
-- are (ss 3, 4), the offences of running one unlicensed and of a driver taking bookings from an unlicensed provider (ss 9-11), false
-- applications (s 12(5)), the cap on the LTA's financial penalty and the 3-month suspension (s 35), notice before regulatory action
-- (s 36), roadside questioning of drivers and passengers and the offence of not complying (ss 39, 41), composition (s 42) and appeals
-- to the Minister (ss 43, 44).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation "version in force from 4/5/2026", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/PPPTIA2019.txt. The cover says the revised edition incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021;
-- the latest amendment annotated in the text is Act 5 of 2026 (wef 04/05/2026, the definition of "motor vehicle"); Act 30 of 2024
-- (Platform Workers Act 2024, wef 01/01/2025) is annotated in s 4.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for everyday-life relevance: it governs the taxis and ride-hail apps people in Singapore use, and the drivers
-- who work through them. SCOPED to what a passenger, a driver or a small would-be operator meets. Not encoded: the licence
-- application and grant criteria beyond the false-information offence (ss 12-13, 18-19), licence conditions and their modification
-- (ss 15-17, 21-23), the content of exempt ride-hail operator orders (ss 24-26), accounts and records (ss 28, 29), codes of practice,
-- directions and emergency directives except as appealable decisions (ss 30-34), powers of entry (s 38), service of documents,
-- corporate liability (ss 48, 49), Regulations, and the savings in s 68 and the Schedule. No Regulations or exempt-operator orders
-- were retrieved, so prescribed fees, periods and the fleet sizes that orders may use are unknown here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Point-to-Point Passenger Transport Industry Act 2019`

-- Helpers (the prelude is not relied on for these).
GIVEN `first` IS A NUMBER, `second` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `first` AT LEAST `second` THEN `first` ELSE `second`

GIVEN `first` IS A NUMBER, `second` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `first` AT MOST `second` THEN `first` ELSE `second`

§§ `3 -- street-hail service`

-- s 3: "street-hail service" means a passenger transport service "(a) provided using motor vehicles which are taxis, 2 or more of
-- which at any time in a year are taxis owned by the provider of that service; and (b) under which any individual can hail or hire
-- on-demand such a motor vehicle when it is (i) standing or plying for hire on a road; and (ii) authorised ... to stand or ply for
-- hire on a road". "Provide" means in the course of business (s 2, s 3).
-- So a person owning a single taxi is not providing a street-hail service within s 3, whatever else may regulate them.
GIVEN `uses taxis` IS A BOOLEAN, `most taxis owned by the provider at any time in the year` IS A NUMBER,
      `can be hailed on the road` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this is providing a street-hail service` IF
        `uses taxis`
    AND `most taxis owned by the provider at any time in the year` AT LEAST 2
    AND `can be hailed on the road`
    AND `in the course of business`

§§ `4 -- bookable vehicles and ride-hail service`

-- s 4(1): "bookable vehicle" means (a) a taxi; (b) a private hire car hired "for use as a whole with a driver"; (c) a motor vehicle in
-- a class allowed under s 101 of the Road Traffic Act 1961 to be used as a public service vehicle "and is prescribed as permissible
-- for the purposes of this definition".
DECLARE Vehicle IS ONE OF
    `a taxi`
    `a private hire car hired as a whole with a driver`
    `a section 101 class vehicle prescribed as permissible`
    `a section 101 class vehicle not prescribed`
    `a privately owned car`

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vehicle is a bookable vehicle` IF
    CONSIDER `the vehicle`
    WHEN `a taxi` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a private hire car hired as a whole with a driver` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a section 101 class vehicle prescribed as permissible` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 4(1): "ride-hail service" means (a) an on-demand passenger transport service or (b) an on-demand ride booking service. An
-- on-demand passenger transport service uses bookable vehicles, the passenger "determines or substantially determines" where and when,
-- and it "does not involve a street-hail service". An on-demand ride booking service includes (a) taking or facilitating bookings for
-- bookable vehicles and communicating them to providers or drivers.
-- s 4(4): "a person is not to be regarded as providing an on-demand passenger transport service solely because the person drives a
-- public service motor vehicle". s 4(2)(b): it does not matter that the provider is located outside Singapore if the journey is
-- wholly or partly within Singapore.
-- Simplification: only limb (a) of "on-demand ride booking service" is modelled; vehicle pooling and prescribed services are not.
GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A Vehicle, `the passenger sets the route and time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `involves a street-hail service` IS A BOOLEAN, `takes or facilitates bookings and passes them on` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `only drives the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this is providing a ride-hail service` IF
        `in the course of business`
    AND `the vehicle is a bookable vehicle` `the vehicle`
    AND (    (`the passenger sets the route and time` AND (NOT `involves a street-hail service`) AND (NOT `only drives the vehicle`))
          OR `takes or facilitates bookings and passes them on`)

§§ `9, 10 -- providing a service without authority`

-- s 9(1): an offence to provide a street-hail service when "(a) ... not authorised to do so by a street-hail service licence; and
-- (b) ... not exempt from this section by an order under section 52". (2) "a strict liability offence". (4) a licensee "is not
-- authorised by its licence ... during the period the licence is suspended".
-- s 10(1): the same for a ride-hail service, where the person is not authorised "by a ride-hail service licence and is not authorised
-- to do so as an exempt ride-hail service operator". s 24(3): an exempt operator's service is "deemed authorised by this Act if it is
-- done in accordance with the conditions of the order".
GIVEN `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the licence is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted by a section 52 order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `providing the street-hail service is an offence` IF
    (NOT (`holds a licence` AND (NOT `the licence is suspended`))) AND (NOT `exempted by a section 52 order`)

GIVEN `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the licence is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an exempt operator within the order's conditions` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted by a section 52 order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `providing the ride-hail service is an offence` IF
        (NOT (`holds a licence` AND (NOT `the licence is suspended`)))
    AND (NOT `is an exempt operator within the order's conditions`)
    AND (NOT `exempted by a section 52 order`)

-- ss 9(3), 10(3): "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding 6 months or ... both and, in the case of a
-- continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $500 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- conviction". Days are whole days or parts of days counted by the caller.
GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unauthorised provision` MEANS 10000 PLUS 500 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment for unauthorised provision` MEANS 6

§§ `11 -- a driver accepting bookings from an unauthorised provider`

-- s 11(1): a driver commits an offence if "(a) the driver intentionally takes one or more bookings ... from the provider of the
-- ride-hail service; (b) the provider ... is not authorised ... by a ride-hail service licence; ... is not authorised ... as an exempt
-- ride-hail service operator; and ... is not exempt from section 10(1) ... by an order under section 52; and (c) the driver knows that,
-- or is reckless as to whether, the provider ... is not authorised". Unlike s 10, NOT strict liability.
GIVEN `intentionally took a booking` IS A BOOLEAN, `the provider is unauthorised and not exempt` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or was reckless about it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the driver commits the booking offence` IF
    `intentionally took a booking` AND `the provider is unauthorised and not exempt` AND `knew or was reckless about it`

-- s 11(2): "(a) ... a fine not exceeding $1,000 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding 3 months or ... both; (b) in the case of a second
-- or subsequent conviction, ... a fine not exceeding $2,000 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding 6 months or ... both".
GIVEN `previous convictions under section 11` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the driver's maximum fine` MEANS IF `previous convictions under section 11` AT LEAST 1 THEN 2000 ELSE 1000

GIVEN `previous convictions under section 11` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the driver's maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS IF `previous convictions under section 11` AT LEAST 1 THEN 6 ELSE 3

§§ `12(5) -- false information in a licence application`

-- s 12(5): an applicant for a street-hail service licence who provides a document or information "false in a material particular"
-- and "knows or ought reasonably to know that, or is reckless as to whether, it is false or misleading". (6) $10,000 or 12 months.
-- The ride-hail equivalent in s 18 was not read in full and is not encoded.
GIVEN `provided materially false information` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew, ought to have known, or was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant commits the false information offence` IF
    `provided materially false information` AND `knew, ought to have known, or was reckless`

§§ `35 -- regulatory action against a licensee`

-- s 35(2)(e): the LTA may "suspend the licence without any compensation for not more than 3 months".
GIVEN `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension is within the LTA's power` IF `months of suspension` AT MOST 3

-- s 35(6): the maximum financial penalty is "the highest of the following": (a) $100,000; (b) 10% of the annual turnover from the
-- street-hail or ride-hail business, from the latest audited accounts; (c) $100,000 for each contravention, where the ground is
-- s 35(1)(a) (breach of conditions, a non-offence provision, a code of practice or a direction); (d) 10% of that turnover for each act
-- or omission resulting in a failure to provide an adequate and satisfactory service, where the ground is s 35(1)(d).
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `breach of a condition, code or direction`
    `inadequate or unsatisfactory service`
    `another ground`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `annual turnover` IS A NUMBER, `number of instances` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum financial penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `breach of a condition, code or direction` THEN
        `the larger of` (`the larger of` 100000 (`annual turnover` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100)) (100000 TIMES `number of instances`)
    WHEN `inadequate or unsatisfactory service` THEN
        `the larger of` (`the larger of` 100000 (`annual turnover` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100)) (`annual turnover` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `number of instances`)
    OTHERWISE `the larger of` 100000 (`annual turnover` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `36 -- notice before regulatory action`

-- s 36(1)(c): the LTA's notice must specify a time "being not less than 14 days after the date of service of notice" for written
-- representations. s 36(5): suspension or revocation does not affect "the enforcement by any person of any right or claim against the
-- licensee".
GIVEN `days allowed for representations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice allows enough time` IF `days allowed for representations` AT LEAST 14

§§ `39, 41 -- roadside questioning and the offence of not complying`

-- s 39(1)(f): an authorised officer may "require the driver or any passenger of the vehicle, or a person in possession of the vehicle,
-- to answer any question ... and to provide any document or information". s 41(1): failing "without reasonable excuse" to do anything
-- so required is an offence, fine not exceeding $10,000. (3): a defence "to prove, on a balance of probabilities," that the person
-- "(a) does not possess the document or information required; or (b) has taken all reasonable steps ... and has been unable to obtain
-- it". (4): "it is a reasonable excuse ... to refuse or fail to provide any information, produce any document or answer any question if
-- doing so might tend to incriminate that person".
GIVEN `failed to comply with the officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `answering might incriminate them` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had another reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved they did not possess it or could not obtain it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not complying is an offence` IF
        `failed to comply with the officer`
    AND (NOT `answering might incriminate them`)
    AND (NOT `had another reasonable excuse`)
    AND (NOT `proved they did not possess it or could not obtain it`)

§§ `42 -- composition`

-- s 42(1): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of ... (a) one half of
-- the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000". (2): on payment, "no further proceedings".
-- Which offences are prescribed is in Regulations not retrieved; the caller says so.
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that can be collected to compound` MEANS
    IF `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` THEN `the lesser of` (`the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000 ELSE 0

§§ `43, 44 -- appeals to the Minister`

-- s 43 "appealable decision": (a) refusing the grant of a licence (s 13 or 19) -- and s 2 says "grant" "includes granted or grant on
-- renewal"; (b) imposing a condition; (c) modifying a condition (s 16 or 22); (d) refusing consent to transfer; (e) revoking a licence;
-- (f) imposing other regulatory action; (g) a s 31 direction "except a direction described in section 31(3)" -- the 24-hour order to
-- stop service during a serious public passenger transport incident. Nothing in s 43 covers an exempt ride-hail operator order or its
-- variation or revocation (s 26).
-- s 44(2): an appeal in writing with grounds, "(a) for an appealable decision under section 16 or 22 about the modification of a
-- condition in a licence, within 28 days after the date the decision appealed against is served; and (b) for any other appealable
-- decision, within 14 days". (5) "The Minister's decision on an appeal is final." (7) an appeal does not stop the decision operating.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusing a licence`
    `refusing to renew a licence`
    `imposing a licence condition`
    `modifying a licence condition`
    `refusing consent to transfer a licence`
    `revoking a licence`
    `suspending a licence or a financial penalty`
    `a public-interest direction`
    `a 24-hour stop-service direction in a transport incident`
    `revoking an exempt ride-hail operator order`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision can be appealed to the Minister` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a 24-hour stop-service direction in a transport incident` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `revoking an exempt ride-hail operator order` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days allowed to appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `modifying a licence condition` THEN 28
    WHEN `a 24-hour stop-service direction in a transport incident` THEN 0
    WHEN `revoking an exempt ride-hail operator order` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 14

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `days after service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `the decision can be appealed to the Minister` `the decision` AND `days after service` AT MOST `the days allowed to appeal` `the decision`

-- s 44(7): the decision "must be complied with until the determination of the appeal" unless the Minister directs otherwise.
GIVEN `an appeal is pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision must be complied with now` IF NOT `the Minister directed otherwise`
